{"chunk_id": "e03349647514", "text": "Markandeya recounts the cosmic origin of a famous conflict. After the dissolution of the universe into a single ocean, Vishnu sleeps upon the serpent Sesha. From the lotus springing from his navel arises Brahma. Two powerful demons, Madhu and Kaitabha, appear and threaten Brahma, waking Vishnu. Through clever speech Vishnu secures from them a promise that they will grant him a boon; he then asks to slay them. Bound by their vow, they only request to die on an uncovered place and to become his sons. Finding no uncovered spot in the flooded cosmos, Vishnu places them on his own thighs and decapitates them. Their son Dhundhu later performs terrible austerities and gains near\u2011invulnerability from Brahma, then begins tormenting the worlds. The sage Utanka and King Kuvalaswa\u2014empowered by Vishnu\u2014march to confront the menace, setting the stage for Dhundhu\u2019s destruction.\nDuring cosmic dissolution Vishnu creates Brahma and slays Madhu and Kaitabha; later their son Dhundhu gains a boon and threatens the worlds until Kuvalaswa marches against him.\nThemes: cosmic creation, Vishnu and Brahma, demon slaying, boons and asceticism, divine empowerment of a king", "vector": [0.016681969165802002, -0.01604762114584446, -0.004514658823609352, -0.0018827950116246939, -0.022026676684617996, 0.021473310887813568, -0.022364094853401184, -0.008934840559959412, -0.010244023986160755, -0.021068407222628593, 0.004663122817873955, 0.007956326939165592, 0.011559955775737762, 0.015237817540764809, -0.004555149003863335, 0.008253254927694798, 0.034767597913742065, -0.015615725889801979, 0.02807321585714817, -0.017694223672151566, -0.015845170244574547, -0.005570778623223305, 0.012315773405134678, 0.021338343620300293, -0.027668312191963196, 0.023119911551475525, 0.024199651554226875, -0.01349673792719841, 0.007362470496445894, -0.01395562756806612, -0.0011092631611973047, -0.0025340125430375338, -0.008718892931938171, 0.004470794461667538,